Subject: [PATCH] editor: End on a paragraph after the first stops before its LF

skb_editor_get_line_end_at() (End, Shift+End, Command+Right on macOS, a
triple click, a drag by lines, Down on the last line) builds the caret at
the line's last grapheme as a global offset: the paragraph's start plus
line->last_grapheme_offset. It gives that caret to
skb__caret_prune_control_eol(), which moves a caret off a line's last
control character (the LF or U+2029 that ends a paragraph) by comparing
caret.offset with line->last_grapheme_offset, an offset in the
paragraph. The two are equal only in paragraph 0. In each later
paragraph the prune did nothing: the caret stayed on the leading edge of
the LF, after it. In an editor with a paragraph per line, End was right
on the first line and one character past the end on each later line;
a letter typed there went to the start of the next line, and Shift+End
and a triple click selected the LF.

The prune now gets the offset in the paragraph, and the paragraph's
start is added after it. Paragraph 0 and lines that do not end in a
control character give the same caret as before.
---
diff --git a/src/skb_editor.c b/src/skb_editor.c
index caeffd1..b127eaf 100644
--- a/src/skb_editor.c
+++ b/src/skb_editor.c
@@ -999,11 +999,14 @@ skb_text_position_t skb_editor_get_line_end_at(const skb_editor_t* editor, skb_t
 	const skb_layout_line_t* lines = skb_layout_get_lines(skb__get_layout(editor, paragraph_pos.paragraph_idx));
 	const skb_layout_line_t* line = &lines[edit_line_idx];
 
+	// The prune compares the caret with the line's offsets in the paragraph; the paragraph's start is added after it.
 	skb_text_position_t result = {
-		.offset = skb__get_global_text_offset(editor, paragraph_pos.paragraph_idx) + line->last_grapheme_offset,
+		.offset = line->last_grapheme_offset,
 		.affinity = SKB_AFFINITY_EOL,
 	};
-	return skb__caret_prune_control_eol(skb__get_layout(editor, paragraph_pos.paragraph_idx), line, result);
+	result = skb__caret_prune_control_eol(skb__get_layout(editor, paragraph_pos.paragraph_idx), line, result);
+	result.offset += skb__get_global_text_offset(editor, paragraph_pos.paragraph_idx);
+	return result;
 }
 
 // TODO: should we expose this?
